0.07
 41
4.3
 71
1
  3
- The front door and the carport door both open into the gallery hall; the hall leads straight to the kitchen, past a built-in bench, coat hooks and a floor-to-ceiling pantry.\P- The stair rises from the kitchen toward the front and lands upstairs be
  3
hind the cobogó.\P- Carport: open bay under the upper floor, open on the street and outer sides; a 9 ft cedar slat gate, a Lueders limestone pier at the corner and one steel column carry the floor above.\P- Lueders limestone ashlar on the outer wall 
  3
of the kitchen and living room. Black calçada rug at the carport door and a calçada threshold under the cobogó (about 58 sf, all under the house).\P- Dimensions to the outside face of exterior walls and the centreline of partitions; areas the same wa
  3
y.\P- Ceilings 9'-6" on the ground floor, 9'-0" upstairs. Doors 8'-0" high; window heads at 8'-6".\P- Stair: 17 risers at 7 7/16 in (10'-6" floor to floor), 16 treads at 10 1/8 in, 3'-3 3/4" clear. Open oak treads with a riser bar (4 in sphere rule);
  3
 wall handrail at 34–38 in; cedar slats on the open side, 4 in max gaps.\P- Shared wall of a pair: 1-hour fire-resistance-rated, STC 50 or better, continuous to the roof deck, with no openings. Windows go on the front, back and outer side only; vent 
  3
the dryer and the bath fans through the roof or the outer wall.\P- Visitability (City of Austin, confirm at permit): a no-step entry, ground-floor doors with at least 30 in clear (the WC door 32 in), a ground-floor WC with a 30 × 48 in clear floor sp
  3
ace, blocking for grab bars, switches at 48 in max and outlets at 15 in min.\P- Bedrooms have an egress window (5.7 sf clear, sill under 44 in). Smoke and CO alarms in each bedroom, the hall and each floor, interconnected.\P- Mechanical closet under 
  1
the top of the stair: air handler and a heat-pump water heater; louvred door, and duct the water heater if the closet has under 700 cu ft of air.
  7
