0.07
 41
4.3
 71
1
  3
- For wide lots where the car parks on a pad: the bay becomes a bedroom suite with its own bath.\P- Drawn for a detached site (L4-D2), so the outer long wall takes an 8 ft slider to the side pátio. In a pair, that wall is the shared wall: no openings
  3
.\P- Lueders limestone ashlar on the whole outer side and on the suite's street wall, as at Casa 01; a calçada threshold under the cobogó.\P- Dimensions to the outside face of exterior walls and the centreline of partitions; areas the same way.\P- Ce
  3
ilings 9'-6" on the ground floor, 9'-0" upstairs. Doors 8'-0" high; window heads at 8'-6".\P- Stair: 17 risers at 7 7/16 in (10'-6" floor to floor), 16 treads at 10 1/8 in, 3'-3 3/4" clear. Open oak treads with a riser bar (4 in sphere rule); wall ha
  3
ndrail at 34–38 in; cedar slats on the open side, 4 in max gaps.\P- Shared wall of a pair: 1-hour fire-resistance-rated, STC 50 or better, continuous to the roof deck, with no openings. Windows go on the front, back and outer side only; vent the drye
  3
r and the bath fans through the roof or the outer wall.\P- Visitability (City of Austin, confirm at permit): a no-step entry, ground-floor doors with at least 30 in clear (the WC door 32 in), a ground-floor WC with a 30 × 48 in clear floor space, blo
  3
cking for grab bars, switches at 48 in max and outlets at 15 in min.\P- Bedrooms have an egress window (5.7 sf clear, sill under 44 in). Smoke and CO alarms in each bedroom, the hall and each floor, interconnected.\P- Mechanical closet under the top 
  1
of the stair: air handler and a heat-pump water heater; louvred door, and duct the water heater if the closet has under 700 cu ft of air.
  7
