 40
0.07
 41
4.3
 71
1
  3
- For homes in a row on a shared drive (the 65-ft trio, L4-T1): the bay runs across the front and the car enters from the drive through a cedar gate. Upper floor as A-103.\P- The street sees a full Lueders limestone wall with the cobogó above it on t
  3
he upper floor only.\P- You enter through the bay on a calçada walk; the living room opens east to its own pátio through an 8 ft slider, and the back wall, 5 ft from the next home, takes a band of high windows.\P- Dimensions to the outside face of ex
  3
terior walls and the centreline of partitions; areas the same way.\P- Ceilings 9'-6" on the ground floor, 9'-0" upstairs. Doors 8'-0" high; window heads at 8'-6".\P- Stair: 17 risers at 7 7/16 in (10'-6" floor to floor), 16 treads at 10 1/8 in, 3'-3 
  3
3/4" clear. Open oak treads with a riser bar (4 in sphere rule); wall handrail at 34–38 in; cedar slats on the open side, 4 in max gaps.\P- Shared wall of a pair: 1-hour fire-resistance-rated, STC 50 or better, continuous to the roof deck, with no op
  3
enings. Windows go on the front, back and outer side only; vent the dryer and the bath fans through the roof or the outer wall.\P- Visitability (City of Austin, confirm at permit): a no-step entry, ground-floor doors with at least 30 in clear (the WC
  3
 door 32 in), a ground-floor WC with a 30 × 48 in clear floor space, blocking for grab bars, switches at 48 in max and outlets at 15 in min.\P- Bedrooms have an egress window (5.7 sf clear, sill under 44 in). Smoke and CO alarms in each bedroom, the 
  1
hall and each floor, interconnected.\P- Mechanical closet under the top of the stair: air handler and a heat-pump water heater; louvred door, and duct the water heater if the closet has under 700 cu ft of air.
  7
